examples.bad:
// This is one file, overwritten, so it costs the same on the ten-thousandth
// run as the first - and a dashboard that shows nothing until you rerun with a
// flag you have never heard of is a dashboard nobody opens twice.

// Obviously the cache has to be warmed first, which is the whole point of
// doing it here rather than in the caller.

examples.good:
// A single file, overwritten each run, so its cost does not grow with the
// number of runs.

// The cache must be warmed before the first read; a cold read returns null
// rather than blocking.
